{
 "id": "fox-ledgedash-attack",
 "name": "Get off the ledge",
 "part": "defense",
 "characters": [
  "fox"
 ],
 "goal": "Get from the ledge onto the stage and hit the opponent waiting there before it can punish",
 "why": "An opponent standing by the ledge punishes the slow ways up: the getup, the roll, the getup attack all leave Fox open for half a second. A ledgedash has him on the stage in a few frames, still invincible from the ledge, and attacking before the opponent has reacted.",
 "switch": "success",
 "reset": {
  "after": "quiet",
  "seconds": 1
 },
 "tutorial": {
  "what": "From the ledge: the stick down to let go, X or Y at once with the stick toward the stage, then R with the stick down and forward to land on it. As Fox can act, down-B.",
  "expect": "A try begins when Fox leaves the ledge and is judged when he hits or grabs the opponent, when it hits or grabs him, or two seconds later. The opponent acts when it sees him leave the ledge.",
  "example": [
   {
    "stick": [
     0,
     -1
    ],
    "frame": 1,
    "hold": 1
   },
   {
    "press": "jump",
    "frame": 2,
    "hold": 1
   },
   {
    "stick": [
     1,
     0
    ],
    "frame": 2,
    "hold": "LD-2"
   },
   {
    "stick": [
     0.7,
     -0.7
    ],
    "frame": "LD",
    "hold": 1
   },
   {
    "press": "R",
    "frame": "LD",
    "hold": 1
   },
   {
    "stick": [
     0,
     -1
    ],
    "frame": "LD+10",
    "hold": 3
   },
   {
    "press": "B",
    "frame": "LD+10",
    "hold": 2
   }
  ],
  "marks": {
   "1": "Frame 1: the stick down. Fox lets go of the ledge",
   "2": "Frame {f}: X or Y, the stick toward the stage",
   "LD": "Frame {LD}: R with the stick down and forward. Fox lands on the stage, still invincible",
   "LD+10": "Frame {f}: Fox can act. Down-B: the shine"
  },
  "lessons": [
   {
    "title": "The slow ways up",
    "text": [
     "{opp} waits by the ledge. The normal getup takes Fox half a second in which he cannot act, and {opp} has seen him start it: its attack lands as he stands up.",
     "The roll and the getup attack are no faster."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         1,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 3
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: the stick toward the stage: the getup"
      }
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "The ledgedash",
    "text": [
     "Let go, jump at once, and air dodge into the stage as Fox rises past its edge: he lands on frame {LD} and can act 10 frames later, before {opp} has reacted.",
     "The ledge's invincibility is still on him as he lands. Down-B then: the shine hits {opp} first."
    ],
    "show": {
     "example": {
      "inputs": [
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": 1,
        "hold": 1
       },
       {
        "press": "jump",
        "frame": 2,
        "hold": 1
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         1,
         0
        ],
        "frame": 2,
        "hold": "LD-2"
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0.7,
         -0.7
        ],
        "frame": "LD",
        "hold": 1
       },
       {
        "press": "R",
        "frame": "LD",
        "hold": 1
       },
       {
        "stick": [
         0,
         -1
        ],
        "frame": "LD+10",
        "hold": 3
       },
       {
        "press": "B",
        "frame": "LD+10",
        "hold": 2
       }
      ],
      "marks": {
       "1": "Frame 1: the stick down. Fox lets go of the ledge",
       "2": "Frame {f}: X or Y, the stick toward the stage",
       "LD": "Frame {LD}: R with the stick down and forward. Fox lands on the stage, still invincible",
       "LD+10": "Frame {f}: Fox can act. Down-B: the shine"
      }
     }
    }
   }
  ]
 },
